(Cell Adaptive Responses - Section 1) Tj
T* (Marker 1 identifies this page uniquely within the lecture.) Tj
T* (Hypertrophy is an increase in the size of individual cells in section 1.) Tj
T* (Hyperplasia is an increase in the number of cells within a tissue.) Tj
T* (Atrophy is a reduction in cell size caused by reduced workload or supply.) Tj
T* (Metaplasia is a reversible change from one differentiated cell type to another.) Tj
T* (Adaptation fails when the stress exceeds the capacity of the cell to respond.) Tj
T* (Persistent stress in section 1 leads to injury rather than adaptation.) Tj
